    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6adf982bece625.96083419\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">In Blizzard's latest episode of the WoW Forever Podcast, viewers noticed a not-so-subtle giveaway that the podcast likely plans to continue past WoW: Forever's launch!<br><br>In the background of each podcast episode, the sign in the back has changed - sometimes hinting at in-game coordinates, sneakily giving away a beta key, and more. Now, for the fifth of six officially planned podcast episodes, the sign has revealed the possibility that six isn't the final number.<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><a href=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306514.png\" id=\"1306514\"><img width=\"600\" src=\"https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/screenshots/normal/1306514.png\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"content-image border\" alt=\"WoW Forever Podcast\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; border-width: 2px;\"></a></div><br>The WoW: Forever Podcast has been massively popular within the community. Consistent communication has been something players have wanted for Classic World of Warcraft, and the WoW: Forever Podcast has felt like an answer to that request.<br><br>While we can't confirm the true extent of the sign's truthfulness - after all, it could just be referencing the final, sixth planned episode - the hope is that this type of communication continues. Blizzard has been incredibly responsive to player feedback throughout the beta, so if this podcast is something players are interested in going forward, they should continue to make that known!</div>\n            \n            <noscript>In Blizzard's latest episode of the WoW Forever Podcast, viewers noticed a not-so-subtle giveaway that the podcast likely plans to continue past WoW: Forever's launch!<br /><br />In the background of each podcast episode, the sign in the back has changed - sometimes hinting at in-game coordinates, sneakily giving away a beta key, and more. Now, for the fifth of six officially planned podcast episodes, the sign has revealed the possibility that six isn't the final number.<br /><br />The WoW: Forever Podcast has been massively popular within the community. Consistent communication has been something players have wanted for Classic World of Warcraft, and the WoW: Forever Podcast has felt like an answer to that request.<br /><br />While we can't confirm the true extent of the sign's truthfulness - after all, it could just be referencing the final, sixth planned episode - the hope is that this type of communication continues. Blizzard has been incredibly responsive to player feedback throughout the beta, so if this podcast is something players are interested in going forward, they should continue to make that known!</noscript>            \n        ",
